<!-- Content template version authority. The exact published version of the content template packages
     (Stride.Templates.Samples, .Games.Starters, .AssetPacks) this engine uses: the Game Studio bridge and the stride CLI
     resolve this version (or this checkout's -devN pack of it), and Stride.GameStudio depends on it. It is the version of
     the engine release that published them, so a later engine can name an older number. Don't edit it by hand: a release
     that includes the samples (release.yml) commits it once they are published, so it always names content that is on the
     feed. A stable engine refuses to name prerelease content. Keep the _StrideCommittedSamplesVersion line shape: the
     release workflows read and write it.

     Kept out of SharedAssemblyInfo.cs so committing it rebuilds only Stride.Assets, not every assembly:
     Stride.Assets embeds this file as a resource (outside its reference assembly, so its dependents don't rebuild
     either) and the bridge reads the value from it. Imported by Stride.Templates.Common.targets (the pack side) and
     build/samples.proj (the samples release side).

     StrideSamplesVersion is the version a content pack gets (before the -devN worktree suffix). It defaults to the
     committed value; a -p:StrideSamplesVersion= global property wins (a release packs the new number before it is
     committed). _StrideCommittedSamplesVersion always carries the committed value. -->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_StrideCommittedSamplesVersion>4.4.3</_StrideCommittedSamplesVersion>
    <StrideSamplesVersion Condition="'$(StrideSamplesVersion)' == ''">$(_StrideCommittedSamplesVersion)</StrideSamplesVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
